{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And she came and stood.</b> That she was always occupied with her needs and not with anything else, so that they would not suspect her on account of her beauty." "<b>her resting in the house a little.</b> A short time." "<b>she rested.</b> That she sat." "<b>And the meaning of 'house'.</b> Like 'booth [sukkah].'"], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:23.824941191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}